{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa Has a Nightmare"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Picking a Color "}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 8}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and provide solutions to problems in a range of social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le08ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "makeover"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "painting the walls, putting in new furniture to make a place a makeover look more attractive"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I've decided to give this room a makeover!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le08ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words to review."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "earthy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "looking like earth"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm painting the bedroom an earthy color. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le08ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bed linen"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the sheets and pillowcases for a bed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You should get white bed linens for this room."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le08ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cushion"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a cloth bag filled with soft material that you put  on a bed, chair or the floor to make it more comfortable"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The cushions over there are for the living room."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le08ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "caffeine"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a substance in coffee that makes you feel more active"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I need to have some caffeine."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le08ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Offering Advice and Solutions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can offer advice and solutions to people. Remember to offer advice politely. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You ought to paint it an earthy color."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You should buy more cushions. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You need to choose something brighter."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You'd better give this room a makeover."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about what is necessary, you use <span class=\"italic\">have got to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">going to have to</span>.</p>  When you talk about what is advisable, you use <span class=\"italic\">need to</span>, <span class=\"italic\">could</span>, <span class=\"italic\">should</span>, <span class=\"italic\">ought to</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">had better</span>."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Perfect vs. Past Simple  "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense to talk about a finished action or event that is connected to the present in some way.  You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past</span> tense to talk about a finished action or event not necessarily connected to the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense to talk about experiences.<br/> When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now.</p> Look at the chart about how to form the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Affirmative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">have</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tried\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Negative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">have</span> <span class=\\\"strong italic\\\">not</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tried\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember you can use the contracted form when speaking:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I have/have not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"=\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I've/I haven't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She has/has not \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"=\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She's/She hasn't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He has/has not \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"=\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He's/He hasn't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They have/have not \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"=\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They've/They haven't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You have/have not \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"=\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You've/You haven't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We have/have not \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"=\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We've/We haven't\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I've decided my room is getting a makeover! (<span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span>)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I haven't picked a color yet.  (<span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span>)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I chose a colour - an earthy brown! (<span class=\"strong\">Past Simple</span>)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I heard from my friend Peter last week. (<span class=\"strong\">Past Simple</span>)"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Present vs. Present Continuous"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When use the Present Continuous tense, we concentrate on the duration of a particular activity. You are aware of the passing of time between the start and the end of the activity. This activity is not permanent."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The Simple Present describes an action that is seen as complete."}, {"type": "example", "content": "That's boring. (<span class = \"strong\">Simple Present</span>)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I need some caffeine first.  (<span class = \"strong\">Simple Present</span>)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm coming over once this room is finished!  (<span class = \"strong\">Present Continuous</span>)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "He's waiting to hear from that PR place. (<span class = \"strong\">Present Continuous</span>)"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Imagine you are giving your bedroom a makeover. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "What did you do?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "What are you going to do?"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write about what I did."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about what I am doing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about what is necessary to do."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can offer advice and solutions about healthy habits. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about what people do or what people are doing."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can discuss experiences I've had or haven't had."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What colors make you feel better when you look at them? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "If you could paint your room, what color would you choose?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Let's review!"}]}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "type": "STI", "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "id": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}, {"correct": 1, "id": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id